__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

.venv/

secrets.*.json

# NOT `.env`, deliberately. Which environment a checkout runs as is TRACKED, in
# environment.json — it holds no secret, and it is worth committing so a clone
# starts somewhere rather than nowhere. `.env` could not be: it is the file
# every tutorial in the world tells you to put an API key in, so tracking that
# NAME would make the safety of this repo depend on nobody ever following the
# convention. The name is the safeguard.

# Generated reports land beside the scenario that produced them. A report is a
# build artifact — the controller and the view are the source, and regenerating
# from the same symbol gives the same file with newer numbers. The scenario
# (.md) is tracked; its output carries live market data and would churn on
# every run, so it is not.
.claude_testing_scenarios/**/*.html

